    "simFile": "sims/modules/m79-quorum.js",
    "authored": true,
    "why": "Quorums make consistency a dial in leaderless systems: of N replicas, a write needs W acks and a read needs R. When R + W > N the read and write sets must overlap, so reads see the latest write — without a leader — while the cluster still tolerates a minority of failures.",
